<p id="mwKA"><b id="mwKQ">Monzo Bank Limited</b>, trading as <b id="mwKg">Monzo</b> (<span class="rt-commentedText nowrap" about="#mwt31" typeof="mw:Transclusion" id="mwKw" data-mw='{"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"IPAc-en","href":"./Template:IPAc-en"},"params":{"1":{"wt":"ˈ"},"2":{"wt":"m"},"3":{"wt":"ɒ"},"4":{"wt":"n"},"5":{"wt":"z"},"6":{"wt":"oʊ"}},"i":0}}]}'><span class="IPA nopopups noexcerpt" lang="en-fonipa"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Help:IPA/English" title="Help:IPA/English">/<span style="border-bottom:1px dotted"><span title="/ˈ/: primary stress follows">ˈ</span><span title="'m' in 'my'">m</span><span title="/ɒ/: 'o' in 'body'">ɒ</span><span title="'n' in 'nigh'">n</span><span title="'z' in 'zoom'">z</span><span title="/oʊ/: 'o' in 'code'">oʊ</span></span>/</a></span></span>), is a British <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neobank" title="Neobank" id="mwLA">online bank</a> based in <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London" title="London" id="mwLQ">London</a>.<sup about="#mwt34" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_4-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:1-4"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-4" id="mwLg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwLw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMA">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwMQ">]</span></span></a></sup> Monzo launched as part of a number of app-based <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Challenger_bank" title="Challenger bank" id="mwMg">challenger banks</a> entering the UK market.<sup about="#mwt37" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5"}}'><a href="#cite_note-5" id="mwMw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwNA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNQ">[</span>5<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwNg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwNw">Originally operating through a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mobile_app" title="Mobile app" id="mwOA">mobile app</a> and a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prepaid_debit_card" title="Prepaid debit card" class="mw-redirect" id="mwOQ">prepaid debit card</a>, in April 2017 its UK banking licence restrictions were lifted, enabling it to offer a full <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Current_account_(banking)" title="Current account (banking)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwOg">current account</a>.<sup about="#mwt40" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Welcome_to_Monzo_Bank!_6-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Welcome to Monzo Bank!"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Welcome_to_Monzo_Bank!-6"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Welcome_to_Monzo_Bank!-6" id="mwOw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwPA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPQ">[</span>6<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwPg">]</span></span></a></sup> As of May 2026, Monzo reported having more than 15.2 million customers and customer deposits exceeding £25 billion.<sup about="#mwt43" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:0_2-5" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":0"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:0-2"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:0-2" id="mwPw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQQ">[</span>2<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwQg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<meta property="mw:PageProp/toc" id="mwQw" data-mw='{"autoGenerated":true}'/></section><section data-mw-section-id="1" id="mwRA" aria-labelledby="History"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="History">History</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1" title="Edit section: History"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

<section data-mw-section-id="2" id="mwRQ" aria-labelledby="2015–2017:_Early_growth"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2015–2017:_Early_growth"><span id="2015.E2.80.932017:_Early_growth" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2015–2017: Early growth</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2" title="Edit section: 2015–2017: Early growth"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwRg">Monzo Bank was founded as <b id="mwRw">Mondo</b> in 2015 by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom_Blomfield" title="Tom Blomfield" id="mwSA">Tom Blomfield</a> and his team.<sup about="#mwt46" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-7" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-7"}}'><a href="#cite_note-7" id="mwSQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwSg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwSw">[</span>7<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt49" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-8" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-8"}}'><a href="#cite_note-8" id="mwTQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwTg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwTw">[</span>8<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt50" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:1_4-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":1"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:1-4" id="mwUQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwUg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwUw">[</span>4<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt53" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-9" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-9"}}'><a href="#cite_note-9" id="mwVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwVg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwVw">[</span>9<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwWA">]</span></span></a></sup> The team originally met whilst working at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Starling_Bank" title="Starling Bank" id="mwWQ">Starling Bank</a>. In February 2016, Monzo set the record for "quickest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowd-funding" title="Crowd-funding" class="mw-redirect" id="mwWg">crowd-funding</a> campaign in history" when it raised £1 million in 96 seconds via the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowdcube" title="Crowdcube" id="mwWw">Crowdcube</a> investment platform.<sup about="#mwt56" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Dawson_10-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Dawson"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Dawson-10"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Dawson-10" id="mwXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwXQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXg">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwXw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt59" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Williams-Grut_11-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Williams-Grut"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Williams-Grut-11"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Williams-Grut-11" id="mwYA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwYQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYg">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwYw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt62" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Turvill_12-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Turvill"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Turvill-12"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Turvill-12" id="mwZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwZQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZg">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwZw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwaA">On 15 May 2016, Monzo was named the 59th top startup in Startups.co.uk's annual Startups 100 ranking.<sup about="#mwt65" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-13" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-13"}}'><a href="#cite_note-13" id="mwaQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwag"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwaw">[</span>13<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwbA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwbQ">On 13 June 2016, a company blog post announced that the "Mondo" <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trademark" title="Trademark" id="mwbg">trademark</a> had been legally challenged by an undisclosed company with a similar name.<sup about="#mwt68" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-14" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14"}}'><a href="#cite_note-14" id="mwbw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwcA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcQ">[</span>14<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwcg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt71" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-15" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15"}}'><a href="#cite_note-15" id="mwcw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwdA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdQ">[</span>15<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwdg">]</span></span></a></sup> As a result, a naming suggestion contest was organised and the new name, "Monzo", was registered at <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Companies_House" title="Companies House" id="mwdw">Companies House</a> under the legal name "<b id="mweA">Monzo Bank Ltd</b>" in August 2016.<sup about="#mwt74" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-16" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-16"}}'><a href="#cite_note-16" id="mweQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mweg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwew">[</span>16<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwfA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwfQ">On 16 May 2017, Monzo announced that over £250 million had been spent through its prepaid card, between 200,000 customers.<sup about="#mwt77" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-17" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-17"}}'><a href="#cite_note-17" id="mwfg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwfw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgA">[</span>17<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwgQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="3" id="mwgg" aria-labelledby="2017–present:_Scaling_up"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="2017–present:_Scaling_up"><span id="2017.E2.80.93present:_Scaling_up" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>2017–present: Scaling up</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3" title="Edit section: 2017–present: Scaling up"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwgw">In April 2017, Monzo was granted its full <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banking_license" title="Banking license" id="mwhA">banking licence</a> by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prudential_Regulation_Authority_(United_Kingdom)" title="Prudential Regulation Authority (United Kingdom)" id="mwhQ">Prudential Regulation Authority</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Financial_Conduct_Authority" title="Financial Conduct Authority" id="mwhg">Financial Conduct Authority</a>, having previously operated under a restricted banking licence.<sup about="#mwt80" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-18" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-18"}}'><a href="#cite_note-18" id="mwhw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwiA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwiQ">[</span>18<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwig">]</span></span></a></sup> The full licence allowed Monzo to provide its customers with current accounts, who up until that point were only able to be offered pre-paid debit cards.<sup about="#mwt83" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:02_19-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":02"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:02-19"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:02-19" id="mwiw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwjA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjQ">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwjg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwjw">Monzo's full current account was launched in October 2017, with its pre-paid card users being asked to move to its new current account.<sup about="#mwt84" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:02_19-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":02"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:02-19" id="mwkA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwkQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkg">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwkw">]</span></span></a></sup> By April 2018, it was reported to have 500,000 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transaction_account" title="Transaction account" id="mwlA">current account</a> customers.<sup about="#mwt85" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:02_19-2" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":02"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:02-19" id="mwlQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwlg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwlw">[</span>19<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwmA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwmQ">In October 2018, Monzo reached one million customers, and was also named the best tech startup to work for by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LinkedIn" title="LinkedIn" id="mwmg">LinkedIn</a> UK.<sup about="#mwt88" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-20" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-20"}}'><a href="#cite_note-20" id="mwmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwnA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwnQ">[</span>20<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwng">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt91" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-21" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-21"}}'><a href="#cite_note-21" id="mwnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwoA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwoQ">[</span>21<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwog">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwow">In August 2019, the company announced that it had inadvertently logged 480,000 customer <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Personal_identification_number" title="Personal identification number" id="mwpA">personal identification numbers</a>, making them accessible to Monzo's internal team of engineers. The issue arose because PINs were transmitted in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Query_string" title="Query string" id="mwpQ">query string</a> of a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTTP" title="HTTP" id="mwpg">HTTPS request</a>.<sup about="#mwt94" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-22" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-22"}}'><a href="#cite_note-22" id="mwpw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwqA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqQ">[</span>22<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwqg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt97" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-23" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-23"}}'><a href="#cite_note-23" id="mwqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwrA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrQ">[</span>23<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwrg">]</span></span></a></sup> That month the company also launched its loan products for customers.<sup about="#mwt100" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-24" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-24"}}'><a href="#cite_note-24" id="mwrw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwsA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsQ">[</span>24<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwsg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwsw">In March 2020, Monzo announced the creation of two business bank accounts for sole traders and small-to-medium sized businesses.<sup about="#mwt103" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-25" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-25"}}'><a href="#cite_note-25" id="mwtA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwtQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtg">[</span>25<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwtw">]</span></span></a></sup> This was followed by Monzo's first loan products for its personal current account customers in April 2020.<sup about="#mwt106" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-26" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26"}}'><a href="#cite_note-26" id="mwuA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwug">[</span>26<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwuw">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwvA">In May 2020, Blomfield announced that he was moving from CEO to president of the company and TS Anil would become the company's CEO.<sup about="#mwt109" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-27" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-27"}}'><a href="#cite_note-27" id="mwvQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwvg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwvw">[</span>27<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwwA">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt112" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-28" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-28"}}'><a href="#cite_note-28" id="mwwQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwwg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwww">[</span>28<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwxA">]</span></span></a></sup> He left the company in January 2021, citing personal pressures heightened by the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COVID-19_pandemic" title="COVID-19 pandemic" id="mwxQ">coronavirus pandemic</a> among other reasons.<sup about="#mwt115" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-29" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-29"}}'><a href="#cite_note-29" id="mwxg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwxw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyA">[</span>29<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwyQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwyg">In March 2023, the company announced that it had become profitable for the first time.<sup about="#mwt118" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-30" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-30"}}'><a href="#cite_note-30" id="mwyw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwzA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzQ">[</span>30<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwzg">]</span></span></a></sup> The following year, Monzo was named to the 2024 <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNBC#History" title="CNBC" id="mwzw">CNBC Disruptor 50 list</a>.<sup about="#mwt121" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-31" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31"}}'><a href="#cite_note-31" id="mw0A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw0Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0g">[</span>31<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw0w">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw1A">Monzo reported its first annual profit of £15.4 million for the year ending March 2024, compared to a £116.3 million loss the previous year. The company also announced to open an office in Ireland to expand into Europe. Revenue more than doubled to £514.4 million due to increased lending and savings products, though provisions for loan defaults nearly doubled to £204 million.<sup about="#mwt124" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-32" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-32"}}'><a href="#cite_note-32" id="mw1Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw1g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw1w">[</span>32<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw2A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw2Q">On 30 October 2025, Monzo announced that its CEO T. S. Anil will be stepping down from the position, after serving in that position for nearly 5 years.<sup about="#mwt127" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-33" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33"}}'><a href="#cite_note-33" id="mw2g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw2w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3A">[</span>33<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw3Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw3g">In December 2025, it was announced that Monzo had agreed to acquire the online <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mortgage_broker" title="Mortgage broker" id="mw3w">mortgage broker</a> Habito, which at that time employed 100 people.<sup about="#mwt130" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-34" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-34"}}'><a href="#cite_note-34" id="mw4A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw4Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4g">[</span>34<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw4w">]</span></span></a></sup> The transaction, subject to regulatory approval and expected to complete in spring 2026, aimed to integrate mortgage advice and broking services directly into Monzo’s mobile banking platform.<sup about="#mwt133" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-35" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-35"}}'><a href="#cite_note-35" id="mw5A"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw5Q"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5g">[</span>35<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw5w">]</span></span></a></sup> The company also received a full banking licence from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_Bank_of_Ireland" title="Central Bank of Ireland" id="mw6A">Central Bank of Ireland</a> and the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_Central_Bank" title="European Central Bank" id="mw6Q">European Central Bank</a>, enabling expansion into Ireland with personal and business accounts.<sup about="#mwt136" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-36" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-36"}}'><a href="#cite_note-36" id="mw6g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw6w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7A">[</span>36<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw7Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="4" id="mw7g" aria-labelledby="U.S._expansion"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="U.S._expansion">U.S. expansion</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4" title="Edit section: U.S. expansion"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mw7w">Monzo announced on 13 June 2019 that it would begin offering services in the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States" title="United States" id="mw8A">United States</a>. The company said that it would distribute about 2,000 debit cards to prospective members who attended events it held in major U.S. cities like Los Angeles, San Francisco and New York City.<sup about="#mwt139" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-37" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37"}}'><a href="#cite_note-37" id="mw8Q"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw8g"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw8w">[</span>37<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw9A">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw9Q">In February 2021, Monzo announced Carol Nelson as the new US CEO, taking over from TS Anil who became Monzo's global CEO after temporarily holding both titles.<sup about="#mwt142" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-38" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38"}}'><a href="#cite_note-38" id="mw9g"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw9w"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-A">[</span>38<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw-Q">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mw-g">After it was told by US regulators it was unlikely to be approved for a banking licence, Monzo announced that it had withdrawn its banking licence application in October 2021.<sup about="#mwt145" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-39" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-39"}}'><a href="#cite_note-39" id="mw-w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mw_A"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_Q">[</span>39<span class="cite-bracket" id="mw_g">]</span></span></a></sup> Shortly after, Carol Nelson stepped down as US CEO.<sup about="#mwt148" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-40" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40"}}'><a href="#cite_note-40" id="mw_w"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQE">[</span>40<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQM">Monzo US exited beta and was fully launched on 1 February 2022.<sup about="#mwt151" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-41" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41"}}'><a href="#cite_note-41" id="mwAQQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQY">[</span>41<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQc">]</span></span></a></sup> Without a US banking license, Monzo operates in the US market through a partnership with Ohio-based Sutton Bank.<sup about="#mwt154" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-42" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42"}}'><a href="#cite_note-42" id="mwAQg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQo">[</span>42<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAQw">On 31 March 2026, Monzo announced that it would be exiting the US market.<sup about="#mwt157" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-43" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43"}}'><a href="#cite_note-43" id="mwAQ0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAQ4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAQ8">[</span>43<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="5" id="mwARE" aria-labelledby="Fundraising"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Fundraising">Fundraising</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5" title="Edit section: Fundraising"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwARI">In February 2016, Monzo set the record for "quickest <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowd-funding" title="Crowd-funding" class="mw-redirect" id="mwARM">crowd-funding</a> campaign in history" when it raised £1 million in 96 seconds via the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowdcube" title="Crowdcube" id="mwARQ">Crowdcube</a> investment platform.<sup about="#mwt158" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Dawson_10-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Dawson"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Dawson-10" id="mwARU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARc">[</span>10<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt159" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Williams-Grut_11-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Williams-Grut"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Williams-Grut-11" id="mwARk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwARo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARs">[</span>11<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwARw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt160" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-Turvill_12-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"Turvill"}}'><a href="#cite_note-Turvill-12" id="mwAR0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAR4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAR8">[</span>12<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASA">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASE">In October 2016, Monzo announced an 'interim' funding round valuing the company at £50M and raised £4.8M in the process, led by Passion Capital.<sup about="#mwt163" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-44" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44"}}'><a href="#cite_note-44" id="mwASI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASQ">[</span>44<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASU">]</span></span></a></sup> This round was followed by a second £2.5 million <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowdcube" title="Crowdcube" id="mwASY">Crowdcube</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowd-funding" title="Crowd-funding" class="mw-redirect" id="mwASc">crowd-funding</a> campaign with the total pledged quickly hitting the target amount.<sup about="#mwt166" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-45" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45"}}'><a href="#cite_note-45" id="mwASg"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwASk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASo">[</span>45<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwASs">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwASw">In February 2017, Monzo raised £19.5 million from <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thrive_Capital" title="Thrive Capital" id="mwAS0">Thrive Capital</a>, Passion Capital, and Orange Digital Ventures, which it intended to supplement with a crowdfunding campaign for an additional £2.5 million.<sup about="#mwt169" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-46" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46"}}'><a href="#cite_note-46" id="mwAS4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAS8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATA">[</span>46<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATE">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwATI">On 6 November 2017, Monzo raised £71 million from several investors in a round led by Goodwater Capital. At the close of the round, Monzo was valued at £280 million.<sup about="#mwt172" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-47" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47"}}'><a href="#cite_note-47" id="mwATM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATU">[</span>47<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwATc">On 5 December 2018, Monzo held another £20 million <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowdcube" title="Crowdcube" id="mwATg">Crowdcube</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crowd-funding" title="Crowd-funding" class="mw-redirect" id="mwATk">crowdfunding</a> campaign, reaching nearly £18 million in funding in less than three hours, and reaching the £20 million goal in just over two days.<sup about="#mwt175" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-48" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48"}}'><a href="#cite_note-48" id="mwATo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwATs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwATw">[</span>48<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAT0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAT4">In 2019 the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BBC" title="BBC" id="mwAT8">BBC</a>'s <i id="mwAUA"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watchdog_(TV_programme)" title="Watchdog (TV programme)" id="mwAUE">Watchdog</a></i> programme investigated Monzo after receiving complaints from Monzo customers who had their accounts frozen or closed.<sup about="#mwt178" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-49" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49"}}'><a href="#cite_note-49" id="mwAUI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUQ">[</span>49<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUU">]</span></span></a></sup> Affected customers complained about the length of time they were unable to access their money.<sup about="#mwt181" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-50" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-50"}}'><a href="#cite_note-50" id="mwAUY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUg">[</span>50<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUk">]</span></span></a></sup>
In a response to this investigation, the company said that account closures take place if the bank "suspect[s] there's financial crime".<sup about="#mwt184" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-51" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-51"}}'><a href="#cite_note-51" id="mwAUo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAUs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAUw">[</span>51<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAU0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAU4">On 24 June 2019, Monzo raised £113 million in a Series F funding round led by <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Y_Combinator" title="Y Combinator" id="mwAU8">Y Combinator</a>'s Continuity fund. This round gave Monzo a valuation of £2 billion.<sup about="#mwt187" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-52" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52"}}'><a href="#cite_note-52" id="mwAVA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVI">[</span>52<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt190" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-53" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53"}}'><a href="#cite_note-53" id="mwAVQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVY">[</span>53<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAVg">In June 2020, Monzo closed a £60 million '<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pre-money_valuation" title="Pre-money valuation" id="mwAVk">down round</a>', which saw its valuation fall by 40% to £1.24 billion.<sup about="#mwt193" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:03_54-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":03"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-:03-54"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:03-54" id="mwAVo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAVs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAVw">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAV0">]</span></span></a></sup> In December 2020, Monzo closed another £60 million funding, including from investors such as for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Novator_Partners" title="Novator Partners" id="mwAV4">Novator</a>, Kaiser and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TED_Global" title="TED Global" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAV8">TED Global</a>.<sup about="#mwt196" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-55" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55"}}'><a href="#cite_note-55" id="mwAWA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWI">[</span>55<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAWQ">In December 2021, Monzo closed a $600M funding round at a valuation of $4.5bn, led by the Abu Dhabi Growth Fund.<sup about="#mwt197" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-:03_54-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":":03"}}'><a href="#cite_note-:03-54" id="mwAWU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWc">[</span>54<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAWg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAWk"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeremy_Hunt" title="Jeremy Hunt" id="mwAWo">Jeremy Hunt</a> was rejected for a bank account with Monzo in 2022.<sup about="#mwt200" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-56" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56"}}'><a href="#cite_note-56" id="mwAWs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAWw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW0">[</span>56<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAW4">]</span></span></a></sup> Staff at the bank have been accused of branding the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservative_Party_(UK)" title="Conservative Party (UK)" id="mwAW8">Conservative Party</a> 'evil'.<sup about="#mwt204" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-57" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57"}}'><a href="#cite_note-57" id="mwAXA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXI">[</span>57<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXM">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt208" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-58" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58"}}'><a href="#cite_note-58" id="mwAXQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXY">[</span>58<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAXc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAXg">In July 2023, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gina_Miller" title="Gina Miller" id="mwAXk">Gina Miller</a>'s <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/True_and_Fair_Party" title="True and Fair Party" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAXo">True and Fair Party</a> was informed that their bank account with Monzo would be closed.<sup about="#mwt211" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-59" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59"}}'><a href="#cite_note-59" id="mwAXs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAXw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX0">[</span>59<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAX4">]</span></span></a></sup> Monzo said that they did not accept political parties as customers, and that True and Fair's account was not originally categorised as such in its application.<sup about="#mwt214" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-60" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60"}}'><a href="#cite_note-60" id="mwAX8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYE">[</span>60<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYI">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAYM">In April 2024, Monzo fundraised £500m in a round involving investors Hedosophia and GIC. Monzo achieved profitability and a valuation exceeding £4bn.<sup about="#mwt217" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-61" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61"}}'><a href="#cite_note-61" id="mwAYQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYY">[</span>61<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAYc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAYg">In October 2024, Monzo conducted a secondary share sale at a $5.9 billion valuation, providing liquidity to employees. Investors including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GIC_(investment_company)?action=edit&amp;redlink=1" title="GIC (investment company) (page does not exist)" class="new" typeof="mw:LocalizedAttrs" id="mwAYk" data-mw-i18n='{"title":{"lang":"x-page","key":"red-link-title","params":["GIC (investment company)"]}}'>GIC</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/StepStone_Group" title="StepStone Group" id="mwAYo">StepStone Group</a> participated in the transaction.<sup about="#mwt220" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-monzo-5.9b-2024_62-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"monzo-5.9b-2024"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-monzo-5.9b-2024-62"}}'><a href="#cite_note-monzo-5.9b-2024-62" id="mwAYs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAYw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY0">[</span>62<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAY4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAY8">In 2025 Monzo was fined £21 million by the Financial Conduct Authority for having inadequate financial crime controls. These included allowing "obviously implausible UK addresses when applying for an account", including Buckingham Palace and 10 Downing Street.<sup about="#mwt223" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-63" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63"}}'><a href="#cite_note-63" id="mwAZA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZI">[</span>63<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZM">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="6" id="mwAZQ" aria-labelledby="Products_and_services"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Products_and_services">Products and services</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6" title="Edit section: Products and services"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<section data-mw-section-id="7" id="mwAZU" aria-labelledby="Partnership_with_Flux"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Partnership_with_Flux">Partnership with Flux</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7" title="Edit section: Partnership with Flux"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAZY">On 28 January 2019, Monzo announced a partnership with Flux to add itemised receipts and loyalty points.<sup about="#mwt226" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-64" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-64"}}'><a href="#cite_note-64" id="mwAZc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZk">[</span>64<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZo">]</span></span></a></sup> In addition to this, the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Application_programming_interface" title="Application programming interface" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAZs">API</a> to create receipts was published by Monzo.<sup about="#mwt229" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-65" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-65"}}'><a href="#cite_note-65" id="mwAZw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAZ0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ4">[</span>65<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAZ8">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="8" id="mwAaA" aria-labelledby="Monzo_Plus_and_Monzo_Premium"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Monzo_Plus_and_Monzo_Premium">Monzo Plus and Monzo Premium</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8" title="Edit section: Monzo Plus and Monzo Premium"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAaE">In July 2020, Monzo introduced Monzo Plus,<sup about="#mwt232" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-66" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66"}}'><a href="#cite_note-66" id="mwAaI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAaM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaQ">[</span>66<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAaU">]</span></span></a></sup> a paid subscription service that attracted 50,000 sign-ups in its first month.<sup about="#mwt235" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-67" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-67"}}'><a href="#cite_note-67" id="mwAaY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAac"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAag">[</span>67<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAak">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="9" id="mwAao" aria-labelledby="Contents_Insurance"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Contents_Insurance">Contents Insurance</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9" title="Edit section: Contents Insurance"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAas">Monzo became the first UK digital bank to launch contents insurance in 2025.<sup about="#mwt238" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-68" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-68"}}'><a href="#cite_note-68" id="mwAaw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAa0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa4">[</span>68<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAa8">]</span></span></a></sup> Research showed 50% of UK renters lack contents insurance, with average belongings worth £12,140.<sup about="#mwt241" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-69" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-69"}}'><a href="#cite_note-69" id="mwAbA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbI">[</span>69<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbM">]</span></span></a></sup></p> 

<p id="mwAbQ">The product features:</p>
<ul id="mwAbU"><li id="mwAbY">Coverage for damage and theft inside and outside the home</li>
<li id="mwAbc">Simple 5-question application process</li>
<li id="mwAbg">No-fee policy changes or cancellations</li>
<li id="mwAbk">Optional coverage for high-value items<sup about="#mwt244" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-70" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-70"}}'><a href="#cite_note-70" id="mwAbo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAbs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAbw">[</span>70<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAb0">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>

</section></section><section data-mw-section-id="10" id="mwAb4" aria-labelledby="Issued_cards"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Issued_cards">Issued cards</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10" title="Edit section: Issued cards"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-default-size" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwAb8"><a href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Monzo_Card_CA.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwAcA"><img resource="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Monzo_Card_CA.png" src="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/d1/Monzo_Card_CA.png/330px-Monzo_Card_CA.png" decoding="async" data-file-width="397" data-file-height="251" data-file-type="bitmap" height="196" width="310" srcset="//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d1/Monzo_Card_CA.png 2x" class="mw-file-element mw-file-upright" style="--mw-file-upright: 1.25" id="mwAcE"/></a><figcaption id="mwAcI">The original design for the hot coral-coloured current account cards</figcaption></figure>

<p id="mwAcM">Monzo initially issued (with partner company <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wirecard" title="Wirecard" id="mwAcQ">Wirecard</a><sup about="#mwt247" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wirecard_71-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wirecard"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wirecard-71"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wirecard-71" id="mwAcU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcc">[</span>71<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcg">]</span></span></a></sup>) a variety of alpha, beta and investor cards to its customers who wanted to be <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Early_adopter" title="Early adopter" id="mwAck">early adopters</a>.<sup about="#mwt250" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-72" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-72"}}'><a href="#cite_note-72" id="mwAco"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAcs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAcw">[</span>72<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAc0">]</span></span></a></sup> These were <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debit_card#Prepaid_debit_cards" title="Debit card" id="mwAc4">prepaid</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MasterCard" title="MasterCard" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAc8">Mastercards</a> which the user could top-up via bank transfer or via an existing debit card.<sup about="#mwt253" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-terms_73-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"terms"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-terms-73"}}'><a href="#cite_note-terms-73" id="mwAdA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdI">[</span>73<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdM">]</span></span></a></sup> The balance on the card could then be spent via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contactless_payment" title="Contactless payment" id="mwAdQ">contactless</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EMV" title="EMV" id="mwAdU">chip and pin</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magnetic_stripe_card" title="Magnetic stripe card" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAdY">magnetic stripe</a> or online. From early on, Monzo has issued cards in a neon "hot coral" colour – initially intended as a temporary measure during prototyping<sup about="#mwt256" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-wired-card-design_74-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"wired-card-design"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-wired-card-design-74"}}'><a href="#cite_note-wired-card-design-74" id="mwAdc"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdk">[</span>74<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAdo">]</span></span></a></sup> – but later, a deliberate decision arising from the success of the "eye-catching" design.<sup about="#mwt259" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-breakthrough-brands-monzo_75-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"breakthrough-brands-monzo"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-breakthrough-brands-monzo-75"}}'><a href="#cite_note-breakthrough-brands-monzo-75" id="mwAds"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAdw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd0">[</span>75<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAd4">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAd8">In December 2017, Monzo issued new <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Debit_MasterCard" title="Debit MasterCard" class="mw-redirect" id="mwAeA">Debit Mastercard</a> cards to all its existing and new customers as the bank began rolling out current accounts. Customers signing up for the current account are issued a Debit Mastercard.<sup about="#mwt262" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-76" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-76"}}'><a href="#cite_note-76" id="mwAeE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeM">[</span>76<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeQ">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="11" id="mwAeU" aria-labelledby="Developer_tools"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Developer_tools">Developer tools</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11" title="Edit section: Developer tools"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwAeY">Banks in the UK currently offer customers limited or no programmatic access to their financial data.<sup about="#mwt265" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-77" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-77"}}'><a href="#cite_note-77" id="mwAec"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAeg"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAek">[</span>77<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAeo">]</span></span></a></sup> Whilst the UK Government is looking into <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Legislation" title="Legislation" id="mwAes">legislation</a> to require existing banks to comply with and adopt standards for secure and open <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API" title="API" id="mwAew">APIs</a>,<sup about="#mwt268" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-78" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-78"}}'><a href="#cite_note-78" id="mwAe0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAe4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAe8">[</span>78<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfA">]</span></span></a></sup> Monzo has already released a <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prototype" title="Prototype" id="mwAfE">prototype</a> API based on the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OAuth" title="OAuth" id="mwAfI">OAuth</a> standard within a year of the company's founding.<sup about="#mwt271" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-79" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-79"}}'><a href="#cite_note-79" id="mwAfM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfU">[</span>79<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwAfc">The company has also hosted four <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hackathon" title="Hackathon" id="mwAfg">hackathons</a><sup about="#mwt274" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-80" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-80"}}'><a href="#cite_note-80" id="mwAfk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAfo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfs">[</span>80<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAfw">]</span></span></a></sup> and previously maintained a "Monzo Developers" <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slack_(software)" title="Slack (software)" id="mwAf0">Slack</a> channel for developer discussion and support. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/API" title="API" id="mwAf4">API</a> allows developers to view transactions and accounts, receive notifications for events via <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Webhook" title="Webhook" id="mwAf8">webhooks</a> and create their own items to appear in the app.<sup about="#mwt277" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-api_81-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"api"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-api-81"}}'><a href="#cite_note-api-81" id="mwAgA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgI">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgM">]</span></span></a></sup> The responses are encoded using <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JSON" title="JSON" id="mwAgQ">JSON</a> which allows for data access in any <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_language" title="Programming language" id="mwAgU">programming language</a> with JSON support.<sup about="#mwt278" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-api_81-1" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"api"}}'><a href="#cite_note-api-81" id="mwAgY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgg">[</span>81<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgk">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt281" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-82" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-82"}}'><a href="#cite_note-82" id="mwAgo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwAgs"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAgw">[</span>82<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwAg0">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="12" id="mwAg4" aria-labelledby="Leadership"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading2"><h2 id="Leadership">Leadership</h2><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Monzo&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12" title="Edit section: Leadership"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>

